## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of Copy-On-Write semantics, page fault-driven memory management, and race condition handling in user-space implementations.

## Key Concepts

- Copy-On-Write (COW) mechanism
- Page table management
- Atomic operations and reference counting
- Memory barriers and synchronization
- Race condition prevention

## Code Example

```c
// Pseudo-code: per-page reference counting with CAS-based cloning
void handle_write_fault(Page *p) {
  if (atomic_fetch_sub(&p->refcount, 1) <= 0) {
    // Another thread already consumed this page
    return;
  }
  Page *clone = allocate_page();
  memcpy(clone->data, p->data, PAGE_SIZE);
  update_pte(thread->ttbr, vaddr, clone->phys);
}
