## Why This Is Asked

Designing a scalable I/O completion path tests understanding of batching, ordering guarantees, and inter-processor synchronization under NUMA. It also probes how to minimize cross-node traffic while preserving per-I/O semantics.

## Key Concepts

- IO completion batching
- NUMA-aware per-CPU queues
- Memory barriers and ordering
- Partial completion semantics and retries

## Code Example

```c
// Minimal batching sketch
typedef struct {
  uint64_t seq;
  struct io_req *reqs[32];
  int n;
} batch_t;

void batch_append(batch_t *b, struct io_req *r){
  if (b->n < 32) b->reqs[b->n++] = r;
}
```

