## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of OS memory management, paging, and NUMA in realistic workloads.

## Key Concepts
- Page fault handling, TLB, page cache
- madvise hints and memory binding
- THP trade-offs and NUMA effects

## Code Example
```c
// C example for memory optimization
int prefetch_dataset(void* addr, size_t len) {
    // Pre-fault pages to reduce page fault latency
    return madvise(addr, len, MADV_WILLNEED);
}

int bind_numa(void* addr, size_t len, int node) {
    // Bind memory to specific NUMA node for locality
    return mbind(addr, len, MPOL_BIND, &node, sizeof(node));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical thinking about read-ahead, IO overlap, and correctness under concurrent readers in a real OS path.

## Key Concepts
- Read-ahead triggers based on access patterns
- Window sizing and IO overlap
- Prefetch state and synchronization
